const pagesPrep = `<details class="prep-details"><summary>Checked Skola Pages prep, in plain words</summary><ol><li>Use the checked prep revision and keep cloud initialization and its UI removed. Local cards stay in IndexedDB. Do not sign in or contact the maintainer's sync service.</li><li>For a fork named <code>skola</code>, the app base is <code>/skola/</code>. The PWA <code>start_url</code> and <code>scope</code> stay under the same project path, and assets must work there.</li><li>Remove the upstream <code>CNAME</code> step and legacy deploy scripts that create it. Do not publish the maintainer's domain.</li><li>Keep LICENSE and notices. Add a dated modified-by note and link the live app to your own corresponding source. Replace reference identity and URL fields with your own.</li><li>Enable Actions in your own fork, then set <strong>Settings > Pages > Source</strong> to <strong>GitHub Actions</strong>. The prepared workflow uses Configure Pages for its base path and deploys after a push to main or a manual run.</li><li>Review and test on a feature branch. Check that the PR base is your own fork, then approve any merge or deployment. Open the live URL in a fresh browser and on your phone.</li></ol><p class="small muted">The local browser checks passed. Tests, type checks and /skola/ builds also pass on public-npm Windows, macOS and Linux runners with Node 22 and 26: all six jobs. Personal-laptop UI, permissions, venue Wi-Fi and a real Pages deployment are separate checks.</p>${skolaBuildCommands('publish-build')}<p class="small muted">Public-npm cold installs took about 10 to 36 seconds on the runners. Venue Wi-Fi will be slower. Allow about 900 MB for the pnpm store plus node_modules, with caches using additional space.</p><p><a href="${DOCS.skolaCI}">Runner verification</a> · <a href="${u('keep-going/#publish-your-version')}">Open the full publishing guide</a>.</p></details>`;
